    {
      "t": "display",
      "text": "Project Description",
      "font": "Jersey 10:Regular 400 48px"
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Burning Out is a third-person co-op survival horror game about being alone together. Players escape the maze's floors as a group, evading its monsters and unearthing its secrets. The only light down there is fire they have to carry, share, and spend.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "It began in UCI's Game Design program, boothed at the Z3 Games Expo 2025, and shipped to Steam under Burnt Out Games. I drove the whiteboard discussions around one question, and we used it as the basis for every design decision: how do you make multiplayer horror actually scary?",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "iframe",
          "src": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/67qtTwK3ETY?autoplay=1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Being alone in the dark is frightening. Being alone in the dark with three friends on voice chat is a comedy.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "So the light became the answer: fire is finite, it burns down, and you have to carry and share it.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Splitting up means somebody walks in the dark. The game never enforces the group staying together; the players enforce it on each other.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Fire is the only resource and it gets handed between players, so every client has to agree about who is holding what.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "I designed and engineered core gameplay, systems and UX, and co-founded the LLC that published it.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "display",
      "text": "What I Built",
      "font": "Jersey 10:Regular 400 48px"
    },
    {
      "t": "sub",
      "text": "Damage and Stats",
      "font": "Roboto:Black 900 24px"
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The tension mechanic is a lighting system.",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "capsule",
      "items": [
        {
          "t": "li",
          "text": "Torch and fire system: dynamic lighting, flame behavior, torchwood burndown, tuned so a torch running low is something you notice before it matters",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        },
        {
          "t": "li",
          "text": "Movement controls and interaction",
          "font": "Roboto:Regular 400 20px"
        }
